{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Frontend Update Reminder",
  "description": "Reminds to sync frontend changes to S3 and invalidate CloudFront cache",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "frontend/*.html",
      "frontend/*.js",
      "frontend/*.css"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Frontend file was modified. Review the changes and remind the user:\n\n1. **API Endpoint Consistency**:\n   - Check if API URLs match the deployed REST API ID\n   - Verify endpoints use correct paths: /restaurants, /equipment, /inventory, /staffing, /tickets, /chat, /chat-stream\n\n2. **Cognito Authentication**:\n   - Verify auth.js is properly integrated\n   - Check for proper token handling\n   - Ensure protected routes require authentication\n\n3. **Security Checks**:\n   - No hardcoded credentials or API keys\n   - CORS handled properly\n   - Input validation on forms\n\n4. **Deployment Reminder**:\n   After testing locally, deploy with:\n   ```bash\n   # Get bucket name\n   S3_BUCKET=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks \\\n       --stack-name restaurant-agent-infrastructure-prod \\\n       --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey==`BucketName`].OutputValue' \\\n       --output text)\n   \n   # Sync to S3\n   aws s3 sync frontend/ s3://$S3_BUCKET/ --delete\n   \n   # Invalidate CloudFront cache\n   CLOUDFRONT_ID=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks \\\n       --stack-name restaurant-agent-infrastructure-prod \\\n       --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey==`DistributionId`].OutputValue' \\\n       --output text)\n   aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id $CLOUDFRONT_ID --paths \"/*\"\n   ```\n   \n   Or use the utility script:\n   ```bash\n   ./deployment/utils/invalidate-frontend-cache.sh\n   ```"
  }
}
